  "hints": [
    "Fix the left and right columns and compress rows into sums: now it's \"best subarray sum \u2264 k\" in 1-D.",
    "For a prefix sum `S`, you want the smallest earlier prefix `\u2265 S - k`. A sorted set (TreeSet.ceiling) finds it in O(log n).",
    "for left, right column pairs:\n    rowSums = sums of each row between left and right\n    seen = sorted set {0}; prefix = 0\n    for s in rowSums:\n        prefix += s\n        c = seen.ceiling(prefix - k)\n        if c exists: best = max(best, prefix - c)\n        seen.add(prefix)\nreturn best",
    "O(n^2 m log m). A sorted set is needed because, unlike \"sum equals k\", you need the closest prefix, not an exact one."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(n^2 m log m)",
    "space": "O(m)"
  },
